    "canonical_url": "https://pandas.pydata.org/pandas-docs/version/2.0/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.items.html",
    "title": "pandas.DataFrame.items — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DataFrame.items#\n\n- DataFrame.items()[source]#\n- Iterate over (column name, Series) pairs. Iterates over the DataFrame columns, returning a tuple with the column name and the content as a Series. \n  - Yields\n    - **label** object\n    - The column names for the DataFrame being iterated over.\n    - **content** Series\n    - The column entries belonging to each label, as a Series.\n See also \n  - `DataFrame.iterrows`\n  - Iterate over DataFrame rows as (index, Series) pairs.\n  - `DataFrame.itertuples`\n  - Iterate over DataFrame rows as namedtuples of the values.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({'species': ['bear', 'bear', 'marsupial'], ... 'population': [1864, 22000, 80000]}, ... index=['panda', 'polar', 'koala']) >>> df species population panda bear 1864 polar bear 22000 koala marsupial 80000 >>> for label, content in df.items(): ... print(f'label: {label}') ... print(f'content: {content}', sep='\\n') ... label: species content: panda bear polar bear koala marsupial Name: species, dtype: object label: population content: panda 1864 polar 22000 koala 80000 Name: population, dtype: int64",
    "markdown_length": 1106,
